{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-62447","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119669","text":"The R0.9 evidence gate: brief AMENDMENT 3 (R130 option b), after Codex's review 1"}]},{"id":"blk-62448","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119670","text":"Written by the supervising Mac session, which owns the brief, BEFORE the follow-up turn. It adds to "},{"id":"spn-119671","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/r09-evidence-gate-brief.md"},{"id":"spn-119672","text":" (sha256 "},{"id":"spn-119673","marks":["code"],"text":"260038bc…"},{"id":"spn-119674","text":", unchanged) and wins wherever the two differ."}]},{"id":"blk-62449","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119675","text":"Ruling on containment (Codex review 1, finding 1)"}]},{"id":"blk-62450","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119676","text":"The static gates stay "},{"id":"spn-119677","marks":["bold"],"text":"in-process"},{"id":"spn-119678","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-119679","marks":["code"],"text":"runpy"},{"id":"spn-119680","text":"), and "},{"id":"spn-119681","marks":["bold"],"text":"no subprocess"},{"id":"spn-119682","text":" stays the rule. The gate's subject is Super's review runner, whose sandbox is the containment: a read-only snapshot of tracked files, no network, and a tmpfs home. The runner's timeout is the time bound. The three static gates import only "},{"id":"spn-119683","marks":["code"],"text":"re"},{"id":"spn-119684","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119685","marks":["code"],"text":"sys"},{"id":"spn-119686","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-119687","marks":["code"],"text":"pathlib"},{"id":"spn-119688","text":", and they write nothing, start nothing, set no signal handler, change no directory and replace no stream (measured 2026-10-02). The gate's own duty is to leave the interpreter as it found it between gates, and to fail closed when it cannot."}]},{"id":"blk-62451","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-119689","text":"Added and clarified laws"}]},{"id":"blk-62452","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-62454","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119690","marks":["bold"],"text":"G0, the reference is the pinned reference (new)."},{"id":"spn-119691","text":" The SHA-256 of "},{"id":"spn-119692","marks":["code"],"text":"lab/r09close/evidence-gate-reference.json"},{"id":"spn-119693","text":" must equal"}]}],"id":"blk-62453","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-62455","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119694","marks":["code"],"text":"b8c6abb2f9eb1900e5604cf8b9426c9af7da580685c9c3851fd7964737ac4002"},{"id":"spn-119695","text":". The gate holds this value as a constant. A missing, unreadable or different reference is "},{"id":"spn-119696","marks":["code"],"text":"G0 FAIL"},{"id":"spn-119697","text":". G1–G4 are still evaluated after a G0 failure, wherever the reference can be parsed."}]},{"id":"blk-62456","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-62458","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119698","marks":["bold"],"text":"The repository root."},{"id":"spn-119699","text":" If the gate cannot make the repository root (the directory above "},{"id":"spn-119700","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/"},{"id":"spn-119701","text":") its working directory,"}]}],"id":"blk-62457","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-62459","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119702","text":"EVERY law (G0–G4) FAILs. No input may be read relative to any other directory."}]},{"id":"blk-62460","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-62462","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119703","marks":["bold"],"text":"G4, exactly these three."},{"id":"spn-119704","text":" The reference's "},{"id":"spn-119705","marks":["code"],"text":"static_gates"},{"id":"spn-119706","text":" must be exactly "},{"id":"spn-119707","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/rendezvous_boundary_gate.py"},{"id":"spn-119708","text":","}]}],"id":"blk-62461","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-62463","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119709","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/nodeid_map_guard.py"},{"id":"spn-119710","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-119711","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/r09_accounting_gate.py"},{"id":"spn-119712","text":", in that order. A shorter, longer or different list is "},{"id":"spn-119713","marks":["code"],"text":"G4 FAIL"},{"id":"spn-119714","text":", before anything runs."}]},{"id":"blk-62464","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-62466","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119715","marks":["bold"],"text":"G4 restoration."},{"id":"spn-119716","text":" Around each static gate, the gate restores "},{"id":"spn-119717","marks":["code"],"text":"sys.argv"},{"id":"spn-119718","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119719","marks":["code"],"text":"sys.path"},{"id":"spn-119720","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119721","marks":["code"],"text":"sys.stdout"},{"id":"spn-119722","text":", "},{"id":"spn-119723","marks":["code"],"text":"sys.stderr"},{"id":"spn-119724","text":", the"}]}],"id":"blk-62465","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-62467","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119725","text":"working directory, and "},{"id":"spn-119726","marks":["code"],"text":"sys.modules"},{"id":"spn-119727","text":" (removing every module the static gate added). If any of these cannot be restored, that is "},{"id":"spn-119728","marks":["code"],"text":"G4 FAIL"},{"id":"spn-119729","text":", naming what could not be restored. Nothing is silently passed over."}]},{"id":"blk-62468","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-62470","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119730","marks":["bold"],"text":"G3's context (unchanged, stated)."},{"id":"spn-119731","text":" G3 is judged on the runner's snapshot of tracked files. On a working tree that holds"}]}],"id":"blk-62469","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-62471","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119732","text":"untracked build output inside a frozen crate, G3 fails by design, and it must not be weakened to ignore such files."}]},{"id":"blk-62472","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-62474","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119733","marks":["bold"],"text":"G5, exact."}]}],"id":"blk-62473","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-62476","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119734","text":"Each of G0, G1, G2, G3 and G4 prints exactly one line, "},{"id":"spn-119735","marks":["code"],"text":"G<n> ok …"},{"id":"spn-119736","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-119737","marks":["code"],"text":"G<n> FAIL …"},{"id":"spn-119738","text":", in that order."}]}],"id":"blk-62475","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-62478","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119739","text":"Then exactly one of "},{"id":"spn-119740","marks":["code"],"text":"EVIDENCE GATE HELD"},{"id":"spn-119741","text":" (exit status exactly 0) or "},{"id":"spn-119742","marks":["code"],"text":"EVIDENCE GATE BROKEN: "},{"id":"spn-119743","text":" followed by the failed laws"}]}],"id":"blk-62477","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-62479","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119744","text":"in order, separated by single spaces (exit status exactly 1)."}]},{"id":"blk-62480","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-62482","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-119745","marks":["bold"],"text":"Unchanged:"},{"id":"spn-119746","text":" G1–G3's definitions, every constraint in the brief, and the two input files."}]}],"id":"blk-62481","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera4o3giijimflcfnyjztmpq7sqr7twtid33wsjkfl76wy6utjxdrba","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}